      "text": "1. JavaScript in Console (Inspect)\n(i) allows real-time editing of HTML/CSS/JS.\n(ii) run scripts : test code in console.\n(iii) debug : locate and fix error.\n(iv) modify DOM : change webpage elements.\nerrors : view error message.\n\nalert('welcome to shamli')\n5+6=11\n55+55=110\n\n2. DOM manipulation :\n(i) change html\n(ii) change css\n(iii) perform actions\n\ndocument.body.innerHTML = 'welcome to tarun'\ndocument.body.innerHTML = '<b>welcome to tarun</b>'\ndocument.getElementsByTagName('b') [0].style.fontSize = '40px'\ndocument.getElementsByClassName('RNmpXc')[1].click()\n\n3. Chrome Extensions :\n(i) create features : add new functionalities to chrome.\n(ii) interact rith web : modify or read webpage content.\n(iii) api access : use chrome's built-in functionals.\n(iv) user experience :\n\n4. programming language : \n- giving instructions to a computer.\n- instruction : tells computer what to do.\n- these instruction are called code.\n\n5. syntax :\n- structure of words in a sentence.\n- rules of the language.\n- for programming exact syntax must be followed.\n\n6. frontend / backend / fullstack :\nhtml, css, javascript                 java, python\nclient side /front-end             service side back-end\nweb development\n                       MERN full stack\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. JavaScript in Console (Inspect)\n(i) allows real-time editing of HTML/CSS/JS.\n(ii) run scripts : test code in console.\n(iii) debug : locate and fix error.\n(iv) modify DOM : change webpage elements.\nerrors : view error message.\n\nalert('welcome to shamli')\n5+6=11\n55+55=110\n\n2. DOM manipulation :\n(i) change html\n(ii) change css\n(iii) perform actions\n\ndocument.body.innerHTML = 'welcome to tarun'\ndocument.body.innerHTML = '<b>welcome to tarun</b>'\ndocument.getElementsByTagName('b') [0].style.fontSize = '40px'\ndocument.getElementsByClassName('RNmpXc')[1].click()\n\n3. Chrome Extensions :\n(i) create features : add new functionalities to chrome.\n(ii) interact rith web : modify or read webpage content.\n(iii) api access : use chrome's built-in functionals.\n(iv) user experience :\n\n4. programming language : \n- giving instructions to a computer.\n- instruction : tells computer what to do.\n- these instruction are called code.\n\n5. syntax :\n- structure of words in a sentence.\n- rules of the language.\n- for programming exact syntax must be followed.\n\n6. frontend / backend / fullstack :\nhtml, css, javascript                 java, python\nclient side /front-end             service side back-end\nweb development\n                       MERN full stack\n",
